{"step_index":369,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T10:29:27Z","content":"Here is the complete step-by-step guide on how to run **SonarQube** on your laptop for this project:\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: Run SonarQube Server locally via Docker (Recommended & Easiest)\n\nIf you have **Docker Desktop** installed on your laptop, you can start a full SonarQube server in less than 2 minutes:\n\n#### Step 1: Start SonarQube Container\nOpen **PowerShell** and run:\n```powershell\ndocker run -d --name sonarqube -e SONAR_ES_BOOTSTRAP_CHECKS_DISABLE=true -p 9000:9000 sonarqube:community\n```\n\n#### Step 2: Access SonarQube Dashboard\n1. Open your browser and go to:  \n   👉 **`http://localhost:9000`**\n2. Log in with the default credentials:\n   * **Username**: `admin`\n   * **Password**: `admin`\n   *(It will prompt you to set a new password on first login).*\n\n#### Step 3: Run the SonarQube Scanner over Your Project\nIn your project directory, run the official Sonar Scanner container to analyze the code:\n```powershell\ncd c:\\Users\\addal\\Documents\\antigravity\\focused-bell\n\ndocker run --rm -e SONAR_HOST_URL=\"http://host.docker.internal:9000\" -v \"${PWD}:/usr/src\" sonarsource/sonar-scanner-cli\n```\n* Once complete, refresh `http://localhost:9000` to view your interactive SonarQube dashboard with vulnerability graphs, code smells, and quality gates!\n\n---\n\n### Method 2: Run the Built-In Python Static Security Scanner (No Docker Required)\n\nIf you don't want to run a heavy Docker server, you can run the exact static security analyzer rules directly from your terminal:\n\n#### 1. Run Security Vulnerability Scanner (SAST)\n```powershell\ncd c:\\Users\\addal\\Documents\\antigravity\\focused-bell\\backend\n\npython -m bandit -r app/ -f txt\n```\n\n#### 2. Run Code Smells & Quality Linter Scanner\n```powershell\ncd c:\\Users\\addal\\Documents\\antigravity\\focused-bell\\backend\n\npython -m ruff check app/\n```\n\n---\n\n### 📄 Configuration File Included\nYour project already includes the pre-configured Sonar properties file:\n* [`sonar-project.properties`](file:///c:/Users/addal/Documents/antigravity/focused-bell/sonar-project.properties)"}
